    {
      "id": "reference",
      "type": "calibration.flat_field_reference",
      "name": "Build median references",
      "documentation": "<p>Estimate bright and dark references from independent repeated-capture batches. Keep camera, optics, exposure, gain and lighting settings fixed; registration and camera-setting verification are operator responsibilities. Alpha does not participate in calibration and is retained only on Source. Saturation rejection is per capture pixel across all intensity channels. Mean/median and optional population temporal noise use accepted captures. Noise is about the mean, also in Median mode.</p><p>Validity requires enough captures in both connected batches, a positive published flat-minus-dark response above the configured floor in every channel, and optional noise limits. Invalid and unselected reference pixels are zero, so correction cannot use them. Floating maps retain original sample units, with no full-scale conversion; choose Raw sample units in Flat-field correction for a different reference depth. Each batch is limited to 64 frames; combined signal samples to 64 million, image pixels to 4,194,304 and each axis to 16384. Reduction uses bounded row tiles.</p>",
      "parameters": {
        "method": "median",
        "minimum_frames": 3,
        "anchor_index": 0,
        "alignment": "pixel_grid",
        "output_depth": "float64",
        "reject_saturation": true,
        "saturation_level": 0.99,
        "minimum_response": 0.01,
        "minimum_valid_fraction": 0.95,
        "check_noise": false,
        "maximum_noise": 0.02,
        "retain_noise": true
      },
      "position": [
        200.0,
        400.0
      ],
      "exposed_inputs": [
        "bright",
        "dark",
        "mask",
        "region"
      ],
      "exposed_outputs": [
        "flat",
        "dark",
        "valid_mask",
        "info"
      ],
      "thumbnail": true,
      "preview_output": ""
    },
